comments.body:
For those interested, I started working on this in this [branch](https://github.com/pedrovrima/supabase/tree/feat/add-schema-diagram). Got react-flow working, and am getting the payload structure and data transformation from supabase-schema to work with.

<img width="1510" alt="Screen Shot 2023-07-09 at 13 31 48" src="https://github.com/supabase/supabase/assets/7888468/5f8ced7c-6ba8-4fc4-b619-46c1cce6ec8f">


@saltcod this is the data structure fetched by supabase-schema (among other objects):

```json
{
    "author": {
        "required": [
            "id"
        ],
        "properties": {
            "id": {
                "description": "Note:\nThis is a Primary Key.<pk/>",
                "format": "bigint",
                "type": "integer"
            },
            "created_at": {
                "default": "now()",
                "format": "timestamp with time zone",
                "type": "string"
            },
            "name": {
                "format": "character varying",
                "type": "string"
            }
        },
        "type": "object"
    },
    "posts": {
        "required": [
            "id"
        ],
        "properties": {
            "id": {
                "description": "Note:\nThis is a Primary Key.<pk/>",
                "format": "bigint",
                "type": "integer"
            },
            "created_at": {
                "default": "now()",
                "format": "timestamp with time zone",
                "type": "string"
            },
            "title": {
                "format": "character varying",
                "type": "string"
            },
            "content": {
                "format": "text",
                "type": "string"
            },
            "author_id": {
                "description": "Note:\nThis is a Foreign Key to `author.id`.<fk table='author' column='id'/>",
                "format": "bigint",
                "type": "integer"
            }
        },
        "type": "object"
    }
}
```

would we get something similar in the dashboard?

@kamilogorek 
[This is an implementation of auto-layout using Dagre library](https://reactflow.dev/docs/examples/layout/dagre/). There are other options as well, but this seems to be the most used one.

The PRO auto-layout example you shared is for adding new nodes, which I don't think is the case for this implementation.

@saltcod I'm thinking to use MySQL Workbench type legends for indicating primary, primary foreign, null, not null & unique keys. My reasoning for going with MySQL Workbench-type indicators is that they've been industry standards for years on years now, and are well-known even with ER Diagrams.

They're indicated by Key, Diamond Outline, and Diamond Solid icons of different colors, however since Supabase uses `react-feather`, there's no diamond shape. Could you suggest where we should source this icon, or if you have any better idea to indicate these constraints?

Sidenote, we should probably have a contributors channel on Discord to speed things up, what do you think?

@AdityaTD - You could add tailwind classNames onto the icons, e.g. for this:

<img width="44" alt="Screenshot 2023-07-14 at 11 40 49" src="https://github.com/supabase/supabase/assets/22655069/ab887d5a-0cf5-4401-9235-57c2ffad5fcb">

The following I used: `<Diamond className="fill-red-500"/>|`
